- ### Finding the annotated field
+ ### Trovare il campo annotato

- Often the question runs the other way: *which* field carries the annotation? When exactly one
- field does, the summoned instance knows its name:
+ Spesso la domanda va nell'altro senso: *quale* campo porta l'annotazione? Quando a portarla è
+ esattamente un campo, l'istanza evocata ne conosce il nome:

= field does, the summoned instance knows its name:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= field does, the summoned instance knows its name:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= field does, the summoned instance knows its name:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(summon[Speech is Annotated by primary].field)
+ Out.println(summon[Speech is Annotated by primary].field)

= Out.println(summon[Speech is Annotated by primary].field)
- ```
+ ```

- Finding the field is usually the first step towards reading or writing it, so the instance also
- offers a [lens](optics.md#lenses-as-values) onto it:
+ Trovare il campo è di solito il primo passo per leggerlo o scriverlo, quindi l'istanza offre anche
+ una [lente](optics.md#lenses-as-values) su di esso:

= offers a [lens](optics.md#lenses-as-values) onto it:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
+ val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")

= val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
- ```
+ ```

= val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= val person = Person(t"Romeo", t"romeo@example.com")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- val identity = summon[Person is Annotated by ident]
+ val identity = summon[Person is Annotated by ident]

- Out.println(identity.lens(person))
+ Out.println(identity.lens(person))

- Out.println(identity.lens.update(person, t"juliet@example.com").inspect)
+ Out.println(identity.lens.update(person, t"juliet@example.com").inspect)

= Out.println(identity.lens.update(person, t"juliet@example.com").inspect)
- ```
+ ```

- This is how a serialization library finds "the field marked as the identifier" without being
- told its name. If more than one field carries the annotation, `field` is not available, because
- the type of the instance records whether the match was unique.
+ È così che una libreria di serializzazione trova «il campo marcato come identificatore» senza che
+ le venga detto il nome. Se più di un campo porta l'annotazione, `field` non è disponibile, perché il
+ tipo dell'istanza registra se la corrispondenza era unica.

- ### Variants of a sealed type
+ ### Varianti di un tipo sealed

- The cases of an [enumeration] or a sealed trait are queried with `under`. The result maps the
- name of each variant to its annotations:
+ I casi di un'[enumerazione] o di un trait sealed si interrogano con `under`. Il risultato associa il
+ nome di ogni variante alle sue annotazioni:

= name of each variant to its annotations:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- sealed trait Colored
+ sealed trait Colored

- @number(3)
+ @number(3)

- case class Hsv(hue: Double, saturation: Double, @ident value: Double) extends Colored
+ case class Hsv(hue: Double, saturation: Double, @ident value: Double) extends Colored

- @primary()
+ @primary()

- case class Rgb(red: Int, green: Int, blue: Int) extends Colored
+ case class Rgb(red: Int, green: Int, blue: Int) extends Colored

= case class Rgb(red: Int, green: Int, blue: Int) extends Colored
- ```
+ ```

= case class Rgb(red: Int, green: Int, blue: Int) extends Colored
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

